memory-graph — code graph engine (.memory-graph/engine/mg_graph/)
=================================================================

Provenance
----------

This package replaces the external `graphifyy` package (Graphify Labs,
https://github.com/Graphify-Labs/graphify, dual Apache-2.0 / MIT), which
memory-graph depended on up to and including version 0.9.36.

**No graphify source code was copied.** `mg_graph/` is an independent
reimplementation written against the same output contract. The two differ
structurally: graphify dispatches through a per-language extractor registry
with caching and manifest/MCP ingestion; `mg_graph/extract.py` drives
tree-sitter directly and supports Python, TypeScript and TSX only.

What is deliberately compatible
-------------------------------

- The output path `graphify-out/graph.json` and its networkx node-link shape
  (`nodes[{id, label, community, file_type, source_file, ...}]`,
  `links[{source, target, relation, confidence, ...}]`). Renaming it would
  break the dashboard and `tests/test_adapters.py`.
- `normalize_id()` semantics, so node ids stay stable across the switchover.

What was intentionally dropped
------------------------------

LLM-written `GRAPH_REPORT.md`; multi-modal ingestion (images, video, PDFs,
URLs); Neo4j / FalkorDB / GraphML / SVG exporters; the MCP server; `--watch`,
`--obsidian` and `--wiki` modes; and Leiden clustering (networkx Louvain was
already the effective fallback, since leidenalg was never installed).

If code is vendored from graphify in future, add its Apache-2.0 licence header
to the file and record the upstream commit here.
